  "notes": "From the street elevation (a symmetrical-ish two-storey front: a white board-and-batten wing on the west, a lower recessed centre with a stone-clad entry bay, pivot door and dark canopy, and an east wing fronted by a two-storey colonnade of five square columns with a balcony between them), the pool view (low hipped roofs on deep overhangs with wood soffits, a covered two-storey porch at the rear corner, a long pool with an in-water sun shelf of loungers and a separate spa, hedges and a black fence) and the article (1,500 m2 on two levels round a central axis). The front faces south. Widths were scaled from the entry door and storey heights (about 4 m each); the plan depth, the side and rear windows, the garage outbuilding's full extent, the pool's exact outline and the driveway layout were not shown and are guessed. The dark standing-seam roof is drawn as 'dark'. Refinement pass (24 Sep 2026): the stacked-slab roofs are now true hip roofs (about a 3:12 pitch, 2.6 m rise on the wings) over a wood soffit band that shows at the eaves; the centre block's hip is narrower and lower (1.5 m rise) so the two wing roofs read as separate, as in the street view; the garage has its own low hip; the two royal palms in the front lawn are palm-shaped and 17 m tall, taller than the house as photographed; the pool now has a pale stone coping and a brown wood-look deck round it (the pool view). Still guessed: the hip pitches (read off a near-level street view), the plan depth, the rear windows, the garage's extent and the driveway. Refined 24 Sep 2026 (three rounds, against the street view 19 and the pool view 10): the hips were too steep - both photos show nearly flat standing-seam roofs whose pitch barely shows above the thin fascia - so the rises are now 2.0 m on the wings (anything lower merged the three roofs into one dark sheet from above) and the centre block, whose eave the street view shows well below the wings', is lowered to 6.6 m with its upper windows shortened, 0.7 m on the centre and 0.6 m on the garage; the board-and-batten walls drawn white (render read grey against the photos' bright white cladding); tropical planting beds added along the front's foot. A thicker wood soffit band was tried and dropped - from above it read as a wide orange rim, where the photos show a dark roof edge."
